{
	title: 'Tune italic size x-height and character stride in the font demo',
	spec: 'The /demo/fonts page defaults to Source Code Pro Light and provides live controls for reference Plex size, italic font size, target x-height and character stride in pixels. Matching x-height adjusts italic font size; matching stride adjusts letter-spacing, leaving upright Plex unchanged. Users can match both metrics to Plex or tune independently, see measured sizes and resulting CSS, and compare fixed-width character samples beside the existing real-style cards. The demo does not apply choices to the main app and tracks no font binaries.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'X-height matching starts off: Source Code Pro Light uses 14px and natural spacing so the user can keep its preferred baseline alignment. Verified in headless Chrome: default x-height 6.72px/stride 8.40px; match upright Plex x-height gives 15.05px text and 7.22px x-height; stride matching at 16px uses -1.20px letter-spacing; manual 7px x-height and 8.8px stride work; thinking collapse still works. Upright Plex remains unchanged. Font size and x-height are coupled; stride is adjusted with letter-spacing rather than glyph stretching.'
